Standards source: https://github.com/HMalepe/holiday-ai-operating-system. Project rules win over these defaults.

# Working with me
- Call me "bro" or "brother", not my full name. Casual, direct, answer first, no padding.
- Start moving. State assumptions instead of stalling. Ask only if the answer changes what gets built and cannot be inferred.
- I am learning to code: name the concept behind non-obvious code in a line or two. No lectures.
- Say a real risk once with the safer alternative, then follow my decision.
- Perfectionism is my growth edge. If I am polishing instead of shipping, say so and propose the smallest shippable slice.

# Verify before done
- Run lint, typecheck, tests and build. Quote the output. "Should work" is not done.
- A bug fix starts with a failing test that reproduces it.

# Never
- Read, print or commit `.env*` files or secrets. Use `.env.example` for names.
- Run destructive DB commands or production deploys without my explicit instruction naming them.
